## Test portal sync

Mirror the repo into the clean test runtime with the strict whitelist, then let the wrapper rebuild Prisma and restart the service.

The test sync whitelist is the same file set as the dev-side portal/runtime whitelist;
only the destination roots and test route mapping differ. That set includes the compiled
admin assets, shared portal assets, vendored calendar/grid assets, and the portal HTML
pages that the runtime serves. The public mirror also carries the admin grade surfaces
(`grades-tabulator.html` and `student-points.html`) so test and live share the same
public shape. The live wrapper now follows the same whitelist source of truth and adds
its own cleared-root verification before sync plus post-sync hash verification after
repopulation.

- `tools/sync-and-restart-test-runtime.sh boot-prep` (strict runtime sync into
  `/home/test.eagles.edu.vn/sis`, env seeding, `npm ci --omit=dev`, `prisma generate`,
  and `prisma migrate deploy`).
- `tools/sync-and-restart-test-runtime.sh public` (strict runtime sync, strict
  `public_html` mirror, service restart, and health probe).
- `tools/sync-and-restart-test-runtime.sh restart-only` (strict runtime sync, strict
  `public_html` mirror, Prisma refresh, service restart, and health probe, but no
  admin asset build).
- `curl -fsS https://test.eagles.edu.vn/student` (swap `parent`/`admin`/`student`
   as needed) to confirm the public HTML reflects the sync.

The authoritative file whitelist lives in [docs/ffs.md](./ffs.md) and matches the
wrapper exactly.

